# cmd.exe parses .bat/.cmd files as a line-oriented format that misbehaves
# around goto labels and IF blocks when a line ends in bare LF (see
# tests/test_launcher.py). Force CRLF in the working tree on every platform,
# including a Linux CI checkout, so the file cmd.exe actually reads always has
# the line endings it requires -- independent of core.autocrlf.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The Python locks are generated by scripts/lock_python_deps.py, which writes LF
# on every platform, and CI regenerates them to check for drift. LF in every
# working tree, whatever core.autocrlf says, keeps a regenerated lock
# byte-identical to the checked-out one. Marked generated so a review collapses
# the hash lists by default instead of burying the manifest change beside them.
requirements/*.lock text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
